  "source_scope": {
    "source": "Only original actual Frame/cfg/Germ/event. StockObservation root, visit, same ledger, original authority, exact source law/current/entry stay installed. No expected next/terminal/physicality/coverage/cancellation data enters target construction.",
    "settled_target": "Observation.Material.target restricts existing Shared.targetAt at the same old event into original full StockObservation material and the actual Shared.nextBorn material. Original target law/sourceState/stepEvent/sourceSuccessor/oldProjection, receipt, firstSuccessor, old/born ledger rows are preserved by that existing transporter.",
    "branch": "compilation directly matches frame.action. inr remains original answered face/consumer; inl emits existing debtAdmission target. compilationFace and U7 audit commutation inspect the same actual branch. No decidable target or impossible next gate is added.",
    "paid": "Original native-write generated nextCurrent and mathNext are retained. The branch theorem receives a local generated paid-step equality, and direct controls generate it from actual Type receipt paid prefix.",
    "settled": "Actual Type Completion.receipt supplies selected settlement; direct gate generates compiles_settled, not_answered and literal_nextBorn without a caller future-positive premise. Both inventory callbacks are read directly.",
    "conservation": "successor_valid consumes active_directlyAnswered_successor_valid in paid branch and active_debtAdmission_successor_valid in settled branch, keeping whole root/current checks.",
    "existing_admission": "Entire StockAdmission old source section byte-identical. Its original compiler/target_current and the original Shared receipt_compiles/receipt_next are directly consumed by the gate.",
    "scope": "This restores actual StockTarget compiler branches and their generated root/current/whole transport. It does not prove original SourceFamily.Runtime.activation already uses these steps, identify sealed histories, compress paid paths, or create physical strict payment."
  },
